Today is Sunday evening.
The doorbell rings and I open the door.
Asha is standing outside.
Moti sees her and goes near the door.
He wags his tail furiously.
Asha comes into the house and affectionately holds him close.
"Maya, thank you very, very much!" Asha says.
"How was he?"
"He didn't cause you trouble, did he?" she asks.
"No, he was a very good guest," I say with a smile.
I give Moti's leash and his bowls back to her.
"But I must tell you one thing," I say.
I show her my slightly chewed sandal.
"He chewed my sandal a little," I say laughing.
Asha looks at Moti.
"Moti, you must not chew sandals!" she says to him angrily.
Asha asks for my forgiveness.
"It doesn't matter, he is still young," I tell her.
"You two go home now," I say smiling.
Moti looks at me and wags his tail again.
I will definitely miss him.
